  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Rewrite each inequation in terms of logarithms, with $x$ as the subject. Then solve it, giving your answer correct to three significant figures.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2^x>12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x>\\log_2 12$; approximately $x>3.58$ (3 s.f. boundary).",
          "worked": "Since $2>1$, the inequality direction is unchanged.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&>\\log_2 12\\\\x&>\\frac{\\log_{10}12}{\\log_{10}2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe boundary is $\\log_2 12\\approx3.58$ to 3 s.f., so the rounded form is $x>3.58$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2^x<100$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<\\log_2 100$; approximately $x<6.64$ (3 s.f. boundary).",
          "worked": "Since $2>1$, the inequality direction is unchanged.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&<\\log_2 100\\\\x&<\\frac{\\log_{10}100}{\\log_{10}2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe boundary is $\\log_2 100\\approx6.64$ to 3 s.f., so the rounded form is $x<6.64$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$5^x<100$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<\\log_5 100$; approximately $x<2.86$ (3 s.f. boundary).",
          "worked": "Since $5>1$, the inequality direction is unchanged.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&<\\log_5 100\\\\x&<\\frac{\\log_{10}100}{\\log_{10}5}\\end{align*}$$\nThe boundary is $\\log_5 100\\approx2.86$ to 3 s.f., so the rounded form is $x<2.86$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$3^x>0.007$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x>\\log_3 0.007$; approximately $x>-4.52$ (3 s.f. boundary).",
          "worked": "Since $3>1$, the inequality direction is unchanged.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&>\\log_3 0.007\\\\x&>\\frac{\\log_{10}0.007}{\\log_{10}3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe boundary is $\\log_3 0.007\\approx-4.52$ to 3 s.f., so the rounded form is $x>-4.52$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
